  "summaries": [
    {
      "id": 876960,
      "category": "team",
      "content": "A null pointer dereference in Node.js X.509 certificate handling could cause the process to crash when converting a specially crafted certificate to a JavaScript object through `X509ToObject`.\n\nAn attacker able to supply or influence certificate data consumed by an affected application could trigger a denial of service by causing the Node.js process to terminate.\n\nThis vulnerability affects Node.js **24.x** and **26.x**.",
